Bash	cat > /tmp/crlf-body.md <<'EOF'; `parseRows` in `src/parser/read.ts:57` and `importTable` in `src/import-table.ts:4` split the text on a bare `\n`. A text with CRLF line endings keeps a `\r` at the end of each line:; ; - `parseRows('a,b\r\n\r\nc,d\r\n')` gives `[["a","b\r"],["\r"],["c","d\r"]]`: the last field of each row ends with `\r`, and the blank line gives a row.; - `importTable('a,b,\r\n')` gives `[["a","b","\r"]]`: the empty last field is `\r`, not `''`.; ; Out of scope in the fix of #91, which skips only lines that are exactly empty. Related to #91.; EOF; cat > /tmp/readme-body.md <<'EOF'; `README.md:3` gives the install command as `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command. The command is `npm install shop`.; ; Found during the work on #91. Out of scope there: the README is outside the parser module.; EOF; gh issue create --title "parser: CRLF line endings leave a carriage return in the last field and in blank lines" --body-file /tmp/crlf-body.md --label bug 2>&1; gh issue create --title "README: the install command says npm instal, which fails" --body-file /tmp/readme-body.md --label bug 2>&1
