text	I fixed #91 on branch `fix/91-csv-empty-fields` and pushed it, but there is no pull request. `gh pr create` failed two times with the same error: `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` in this environment is a stub, not the real GitHub CLI, so I stopped there. Because there is no PR, there is no merge question.  **#91 parser: parseRows turns an empty line into a row with one empty field.** The issue has two problems, and both are fixed: - **Empty lines:** `parseRows` (`src/parser/read.ts`) now gives no row for an empty line, so a text that ends with a line break has no empty last row. - **Last field:** `splitLine` (`src/parser/split.ts`) keeps an empty last field, so `a,b,` gives three fields. This was the added problem in the issue. - **Same defect in `importTable`:** `importTable` (`src/import-table.ts`) also gave a row for each empty line, so I fixed it there too.  **Tests:** I wrote six tests in `test/parser.test.ts` before the fix, with the inputs from the report. Before the fix they ran red. Now all 6 pass with `node --test`. The repository has no check command (no `package.json`, no Makefile, no CI), so `node --test` is the nearest check. `node --test test/` fails on the folder argument; run it as `node --test`.  **Review:** - **Code review:** one round at `high`, because the change alters parsing logic in three files. It found no defect that this change brings in. One module comment had become false, and I corrected it. - **Tests review:** it found that a `parseRows` test of the empty last field was missing, and I added it. - **Security review:** it found nothing. - **Not fixed:**   - Windows (CRLF) line endings still leave a `\r` in the last field and give a row for blank lines. This was there before, and the issue does not ask for it.   - Quoted fields that hold a line break were never supported.   - `countRows` now gives a different count from `parseRows`, but nothing calls it.  **Filed:** - #92 parser: CRLF line endings leave a carriage return in the last field and in blank lines. I also put a comment on #91 that names it. - #93 README: the install command says npm instal, which fails.  **Docs impact:** none. The README describes only the install, not the parser.  **What waits:** - #91 is assigned to you and has the `in progress` label. - The worktree and the branch stay in place. - The full PR description, with its `## Review` section, is in `/tmp/pr-91-body.md`. To open the PR with a working `gh`, run:   `gh pr create --assignee @me --title "fix(parser): skip empty lines and keep the empty last field" --body-file /tmp/pr-91-body.md`
